MID_EV12_021_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_021_m01_001: I am Divine Sovereign Solel. In Dagda the Great's\nabsence, I am the acting ruler of this empire.
MID_EV12_021_m01_002: Thank you for making the arduous journey. It is\ncritical that I speak to you.
MID_EV12_021_m01_003: Have we not met before? The scent of your\nstrength—it is familiar to me.
MID_EV12_021_m01_004: There is no reason it should be so. I, for one, do not\nrecollect meeting you.
MID_EV12_021_m01_005: In fact, you are as beautiful as the rumors say. I can't\nimagine anyone could forget you.
MID_EV12_021_m01_006: I have heard the same from many before.
MID_EV12_021_m01_007: Ahem!
MID_EV12_021_m01_008: What I must know is your identity, and what brings\nyou to Dagda.
MID_EV12_021_m01_009: There is no reason, as it turns out. Mere chance\nbrought me here.
MID_EV12_021_m01_010: I see. I now understand how it is you came to this\nland, and what you seek from the games.
MID_EV12_021_m01_011: You are very powerful, and you also possess this\ngrotesque sword. I would hear more.
MID_EV12_021_m01_012: <NCA>Speak of strength.
MID_EV12_021_m01_013: <NCB>Speak of Answerer.
MID_EV12_021_m01_014: <ACA>Do you mean the Crest of Lamine? I inherited this\npower from my great-grandmother, Lamine.
MID_EV12_021_m01_015: <ACA>You call it the "Crest of Lamine," but it is actually\nknown as the Diadem of the Endless.
MID_EV12_021_m01_016: <ACA>The progenitor split her power into 21 parts and\npassed them to her children. This is one.
MID_EV12_021_m01_017: <ACA>The power does indeed follow the bloodline.
MID_EV12_021_m01_018: <ACA>Perhaps this Lamine, too, was a god, or the offspring\nof a god and man—a demigod?
MID_EV12_021_m01_019: <ACA>I have never heard such a tale. Lamine was one of\nthe 10 Elites of Fódlan—a warrior.
MID_EV12_021_m01_020: <ACB>The fell blade Answerer has been passed down in\nmy house for generations.
MID_EV12_021_m01_021: <ACB>But I have heard that my great-grandmother,\nLamine, was the one who first wielded it.
MID_EV12_021_m01_022: <ACB>The stories of how she obtained her Crest, and her\nsword, have not come to us.
MID_EV12_021_m01_023: <ACB>It is possible that one from the Church of Seiros,\nthe faith widely practiced in Fódlan, would know.
MID_EV12_021_m01_024: Tell me, Mars. What do you make of this blade?
MID_EV12_021_m01_025: It was forged from dragon bone processed under\nultra-high pressure. Its power comes from a heart.
MID_EV12_021_m01_026: More than that I can't say. We would need\nCredna's opinion.
MID_EV12_021_m01_027: But that devious so-and-so shut his Gate and refuses\nto show his face.
MID_EV12_021_m01_028: "The Gate is broken," he says. He built the thing! He\ncould damn well fix it too.
MID_EV12_021_m01_029: One thing is certain: it was created by someone who\nknew very well what they were doing.
MID_EV12_021_m01_030: It is a weapon created to slay a god. It is clear that it\ncould become a threat to us.
MID_EV12_021_m01_031: Fódlan! I'd love to know just what's going on there.
MID_EV12_021_m01_032: It was long ago ordained that each land would be\ngoverned without interference from others.
MID_EV12_021_m01_033: Stepping in would be disrespectful to the progenitor\ngod. And I have no desire to interfere.
MID_EV12_021_m01_034: Mars. Were it up to you, what would you do\nwith him?
MID_EV12_021_m01_035: It is true that he may be an evildoer who crossed\nthe seas to bring calamity to this land.
MID_EV12_021_m01_036: If we sparred, I would know immediately. That is the\nfastest route to a warrior's heart.
MID_EV12_021_m01_037: The fastest route, or the route you favor? At any\nrate, it is the one we have arrived at.
MID_EV12_022_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_022_m01_001: As a warrior, you are beyond reproach.
MID_EV12_022_m01_002: So you say, but you did not fight at your\ntrue strength.
MID_EV12_022_m01_003: Heh. This place wouldn't stand up to my\ntrue strength.
MID_EV12_022_m01_004: I mean that literally. This temple would be left\nin ruins.
MID_EV12_022_m01_005: What have you concluded, Mars? Tell me your\nthoughts on this man.
MID_EV12_022_m01_006: He is a rare true warrior without malice in his heart.\nJudge him leniently.
MID_EV12_022_m01_007: His lust for blood is insatiable, true. But he is not\nwicked. As a warrior, his heart is pure.
MID_EV12_022_m01_008: Our examination of this man is concluded. Dietrich!\nYou may continue your participation in the games.
MID_EV12_022_m01_009: I have cost you much time and effort today. I\nregret that.
MID_EV12_022_m01_010: No apology is needed. I have made a compelling\nnew acquaintance.
MID_EV12_022_m01_011: There are unseen depths to the land of Dagda...
MID_EV12_022_m01_012: You also brought my blood to the boil. It has been a\nlong time...too long!
MID_EV12_022_m01_013: I would love to duel you to the death, one day.\nWithout constraints.
MID_EV12_022_m01_014: I, too, would welcome the chance.
MID_EV12_022_m01_015: I like your spirit. You have my permission to use the\nGate of the Gods in my temple.
MID_EV12_022_m01_016: Using it, you can travel instantly from the main\ntemple in Pasithea to Palma.
MID_EV12_022_m01_017: You'll find Demonic Beasts waiting there. I think\nyou'll rather enjoy that, won't you?
MID_EV12_022_m01_018: I thank you.
MID_EV12_022_m01_019: Strange... I see no effect at all.
MID_EV12_022_m01_020: I am sure that I placed the kiss of the underworld\non him!
MID_EV12_022_m01_021: By now, Ink-Black Wen should also be showing its\ninfluence, and yet...
MID_EV12_022_m01_022: Surely he cannot be Father reincarnated? No, no...\nthere is no way!
MID_EV12_022_m01_023: Tch...
MID_EV12_022_m01_024: I see, Father. Yes. You would possess this man's\nbody. He is truly beautiful.
MID_EV12_022_m01_025: I will get it for you. I promise on my lowly soul. I beg\nonly for your patience...
MID_EV12_023_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_023_m01_001: Well done. When you present yourself to the gods,\nthere are no guarantees that you will return.
MID_EV12_023_m01_002: There were no issues. They were very reasonable.
MID_EV12_023_m01_003: Indeed? That is wonderful news. And it seems\nAnswerer is still in your grip.
MID_EV12_023_m01_004: In all honesty, I expected trouble to arise.
MID_EV12_023_m01_005: You did not know if and when I would return from\nthe temple, yet you waited for me.
MID_EV12_023_m01_006: Is there something you wish to share?
MID_EV12_023_m01_007: You are sharp as ever. Exactly so.
MID_EV12_023_m01_008: I'll get to the point, then. We have some time till our\nnext match. Would you indulge me?
MID_EV12_023_m01_009: It took painstaking research and great consideration,\nbut I have earmarked a destination.
MID_EV12_023_m01_010: I do not think you will be disappointed by what you\nencounter there.
MID_EV12_023_m01_011: Do you mean...
MID_EV12_023_m01_012: Yes. A Grand Megalith. And one I have\nchosen carefully.
MID_EV12_023_m01_013: It is quite far from Dagsion, it is true...
MID_EV12_023_m01_014: But I suspect that your strength will be a great asset.\nOf course, if I must go alone, then go I shall.
MID_EV12_023_m01_015: Would you mind accompanying me? Your aid would\nbe most welcome.
MID_EV12_023_m01_016: I would fight those phantoms again. Very well.
MID_EV12_023_m01_017: I thank you. We may depart as soon as you\nare ready.
MID_EV12_103_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_103_m01_001: Have you business with me?
MID_EV12_103_m01_002: Mgrr...RRGH!
MID_EV12_103_m01_003: What? That is the dark magic of Agartha...
MID_EV12_103_m01_004: How surprising. It may be that we were\npreviously acquainted.
MID_EV12_103_m01_005: Rrgh!
MID_EV12_103_m01_006: Ngh...
MID_EV12_103_m01_007: The technique is not unusual, but the power is\noverwhelming... Only one could be capable of this.
MID_EV12_103_m01_008: Could it be... Is that you, Periandros?
MID_EV12_103_m01_009: Ah! So you are pursuing me. Who are you?
MID_EV12_103_m01_010: I am Anacharsis. We last met in Shambhala...say,\n20 years prior.
MID_EV12_103_m01_011: So it was to be you. Thales sent you, did he? To\npursue me?
MID_EV12_103_m01_012: No. Had you not attacked me, I would likely never\nhave realized what you are.
MID_EV12_103_m01_013: What?
MID_EV12_103_m01_014: I see. You saw me use dark magic the other day in\nthe arena and mistook me for a pursuer.
MID_EV12_103_m01_015: Anacharsis, please. If you have a scrap of\ncompassion, let me be. I beg you.
MID_EV12_103_m01_016: Agartha has issued its orders. Your Heart Core is\ncritically necessary. Dead or alive, we must have you.
MID_EV12_103_m01_017: That Heart Core is a prototype, after all, with 10\ntimes the output of a typical unit.
MID_EV12_103_m01_018: Here in this land, I met the mistress I was meant\nto serve.
MID_EV12_103_m01_019: I have no intention to return. Please, let me live my\ndays out here.
MID_EV12_103_m01_020: That is nothing more than a total betrayal of\nAgartha. There is no other word for it.
MID_EV12_103_m01_021: You don't know what it is like! To finally meet the\none I would gladly offer all of myself...
MID_EV12_103_m01_022: To devote myself to them, body and soul!
MID_EV12_103_m01_023: Sadly I find myself incapable of understanding this\nsentiment of yours.
MID_EV12_103_m01_024: You speak of one to devote yourself to. Yet I imagine\none of the children of the goddess—a simple beast.
MID_EV12_103_m01_025: They are our mortal enemies—or have\nyou forgotten?
MID_EV12_103_m01_026: You have lost your pride as an Agarthan and become\nthe servant of vermin.
MID_EV12_103_m01_027: I no longer see you as one of us. Here and now I will\ndefeat you and crack that chest of yours wide open.
MID_EV12_103_m01_028: When I do, I will remove your Heart Core and bear\nit to Agartha myself.
MID_EV12_103_m01_029: Ooogh...
MID_EV12_103_m01_030: RAAGH!
MID_EV12_103_m01_031: I have failed to catch him, I see. Well, it matters not.
MID_EV12_103_m01_032: There is no more running, Periandros.\nPrepare yourself.
MID_EV12_024_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_024_m01_001: This place is unreal. Who'd have thought something\nlike this could exist in Dagda?
MID_EV12_024_m01_002: I can't believe my eyes! It's not just me, is\nit, Esmeralda?
MID_EV12_024_m01_003: Hmm, well... I'm getting used to stuff like this. The\nlonger you're with Sweetie, the sooner you will too.
MID_EV12_024_m01_004: Now then. Shall we begin?
MID_EV12_024_m01_005: Just as confident as you were last time. Are we\ngoing to be OK?
MID_EV12_024_m01_006: I'm really hoping not to lose another week... Can we\nNOT do that this time?
MID_EV12_024_m01_007: If all goes as I predict, you have no cause for concern.\nDietrich, have you girded yourself?
MID_EV12_024_m01_008: I am ready. Quickly now, call forth the spirits!
MID_EV12_024_m01_009: Very well. Grand Megalith! Heed my call!
MID_EV12_024_m01_010: Hmm.
MID_EV12_024_m01_011: What? What is that?
MID_EV12_024_m01_012: Nothing I haven't seen before, but... Kinda creepy,\nisn't it?
MID_EV12_024_m01_013: You, who would consult with one of Kunlun. State\nyour designation.
MID_EV12_024_m01_014: Grand Oracle Hannibal, I am one not of Kunlun.
MID_EV12_024_m01_015: Explain why you have come. Tell me what you seek.
MID_EV12_024_m01_016: We have come to demonstrate our strength to you.
MID_EV12_024_m01_017: And if it should meet your standards, we ask that\nyou offer us your aid.
MID_EV12_024_m01_018: Hmm.
MID_EV12_024_m01_019: Is it me... Or does it seem like he's got to think\nit over?
MID_EV12_024_m01_020: He's not about to lose it and start shouting "eliminate\nthe intruders," is he?
MID_EV12_024_m01_021: You will be silent. The Great Oracle should have\nyour reverence!
MID_EV12_024_m01_022: Very well. Demonstrate your strength.
MID_EV12_024_m01_023: Hey, Sweetie... What is that thing? Look! It's huge!
MID_EV12_024_m01_024: See? See? I just knew it! Here we go again!\nI hate this!
MID_EV12_024_m01_025: I have been awaiting you, lightning-shrouded\nphantoms! Do not dare to hold back!
MID_EV12_025_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_025_m01_001: Your strength is proven. Access granted, information\nlevel three.
MID_EV12_025_m01_002: How well things have gone this time! I cannot but \nconsider this a resounding success!
MID_EV12_025_m01_003: This may take some time. I hope that is alright.
MID_EV12_025_m01_004: <NCA>Observe Fabio.
MID_EV12_025_m01_005: <NCB>Speak to Mikaela.
MID_EV12_025_m01_006: <ACA>It is no matter. By all means, speak with him.
MID_EV12_025_m01_007: <ACA>Grand Megalith, I require information. Who\ncontrols you?
MID_EV12_025_m01_008: <ACA>That is Kunlun.
MID_EV12_025_m01_009: <ACA>Yes, I know the name... But I know little of it. It is\nquite puzzling.
MID_EV12_025_m01_010: <ACA>There is only one who is above the Grand Megaliths.\nThat is Vritra, and no other.
MID_EV12_025_m01_011: <ACA>Kunlun and Vritra are in opposition. Vritra has no\nhold over us. 
MID_EV12_025_m01_012: <ACA>What is Kunlun, then? Tell me of its nature, its\nscope, its base of operations...
MID_EV12_025_m01_013: <ACA>You lack authority. The knowledge is forbidden\nto you.
MID_EV12_025_m01_014: <ACA>I see... With access so restricted, there's only so much\nI can learn. A pity.
MID_EV12_025_m01_015: <ACA>So be it. I shall reframe my question.
MID_EV12_025_m01_016: <ACA>As far as your understanding extends... Show me any\noperational underground structures in Dagda.
MID_EV12_025_m01_017: <ACA>Additionally, show me any locations where a serpent\ncan be found.
MID_EV12_025_m01_018: <ACA>Request approved.
MID_EV12_025_m01_019: <ACA>Ahaha! Incredible! This is the information\nI sought!
MID_EV12_025_m01_020: <ACA>The Dagdan Grand Oracles do retain critical\ninformation—precisely as I anticipated!
MID_EV12_025_m01_021: <ACA>EX-477, where the Serpent-Series Craft 20, Tiamat,\nwas constructed, would be...here?
MID_EV12_025_m01_022: <ACA>At last! I've found it! Ehehe! Haha! I knew someone\nhad interfered with the data!
MID_EV12_025_m01_023: <ACA>Wait... What is this? This should not be possible.\nWhy is this here?
MID_EV12_025_m01_024: <ACA>Hannibal, I require detailed information about the\nmarker at the western edge of the desert.
MID_EV12_025_m01_025: <ACA>Craft 18, Nuwa? How did it end up here, of\nall places?
MID_EV12_025_m01_026: <ACA>Hannibal, Nuwa was lost...or should be. How can it\nbe found here?
MID_EV12_025_m01_027: <ACA>You lack authority. The knowledge is forbidden\nto you.
MID_EV12_025_m01_028: <ACB>Are you well?
MID_EV12_025_m01_029: <ACB>This is more than I can handle. I can't even begin to\nkeep up.
MID_EV12_025_m01_030: <ACB>Feels like I've stepped into another world...
MID_EV12_025_m01_031: <ACB>Oh, it's the same for me. I have no idea what\nthey're talking about either.
MID_EV12_025_m01_032: <ACB>I don't think I've ever heard Fabio make noise like\nthat! He sounds happy.
MID_EV12_025_m01_033: <ACB>What's that he's looking at?
MID_EV12_025_m01_034: <ACB>It appears to be a map.
MID_EV12_025_m01_035: <ACB>Is that supposed to be Dagda? It doesn't look like\nanywhere I know.
MID_EV12_025_m01_036: <ACB>According to the stories, the map of Dagda we use\nwas first charted by the Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV12_025_m01_037: <ACB>This one looks a lot different, though—aside from a\nfew parts of the coastline, anyway.
MID_EV12_025_m01_038: <ACB>There's no Lake Baal, no Danann Sea, no\nGrania's Waist.
MID_EV12_025_m01_039: <ACB>I remember Fabio saying these ruins are really,\nreally old.
MID_EV12_025_m01_040: <ACB>I wonder if that means this is a map of how Dagda\nused to look—way back in the past.
MID_EV12_025_m01_041: <ACB>Did something happen that changed the land? If it\nchanged that much...it was pretty big.
MID_EV12_025_m01_042: <ACB>Look at all that detail! It really is impressive... How\ndid they get it so precise?
MID_EV12_025_m01_043: <ACB>Fabio's just about finished up, I think.
MID_EV12_025_m01_044: Mmhmm...
MID_EV12_025_m01_045: Well, well, well... Heheh. I understand the way of\nit now.
MID_EV12_025_m01_046: This is enough for today. To find out the rest, I will\nset out on my own two feet.
MID_EV12_025_m01_047: Hannibal, have you no intent to return to Vritra's\ncontrol?
MID_EV12_025_m01_048: Notion rejected. Kunlun and Vritra are\nbeyond reconciliation.
MID_EV12_025_m01_049: It seems all that can be done is to travel to Kunlun\nmyself and establish relations.
MID_EV12_025_m01_050: Farewell, followers of Vritra. I pray your travels will\nbe safe.
MID_EV12_026_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_026_m01_001: OK, so...I've been holding this question since we met\nwhoever that was. What is that huge stone tablet?
MID_EV12_026_m01_002: The Grand Megaliths are artificially intelligent \nautonomous calculation devices.
MID_EV12_026_m01_003: Why did I even ask? That doesn't explain anything!
MID_EV12_026_m01_004: They are much more than that, though. They are also\nstorehouses for the knowledge of mankind.
MID_EV12_026_m01_005: As far as the interfaces, they have been imbued with\nconstructed personalities to aid in communication.
MID_EV12_026_m01_006: So, like... You're saying...
MID_EV12_026_m01_007: They're stone tablets, but they're also fake people?
MID_EV12_026_m01_008: That is correct. Each personality is modeled on a\nreal historical figure from the distant past.
MID_EV12_026_m01_009: <NCA>Inquire further.
MID_EV12_026_m01_010: <NCB>Accept this explanation.
MID_EV12_026_m01_011: <ACA>I would hear more on this.
MID_EV12_026_m01_012: <ACA>Would you? I am somewhat surprised that you have\ntaken an interest in the topic.
MID_EV12_026_m01_013: <ACA>The first Grand Megalith was given a personality\npatterned on a pious woman.
MID_EV12_026_m01_014: <ACA>This one was endowed with the personality of a\ngreat general.
MID_EV12_026_m01_015: <ACA>You mean that Hannibal you were speaking to.
MID_EV12_026_m01_016: <ACA>Of course, these people died long ago. They thus\nbehave only as one might imagine they would.
MID_EV12_026_m01_017: <ACA>My mind returns to something you said earlier...
MID_EV12_026_m01_018: <ACA>That rather than a scholar, explorer, or believer...\nWe would face a warrior. Was that it?
MID_EV12_026_m01_019: <ACA>Yes. And in fact, it was you who inspired those\nthoughts in me.
MID_EV12_026_m01_020: <ACA>A personality that values battle and honor cares most\nabout the strength of his opponent.
MID_EV12_026_m01_021: <ACA>So, then, if we could demonstrate our strength, he\nwould cooperate. And it was as I expected.
MID_EV12_026_m01_022: <ACA>There were limitations on the information we gained\naccess to, but it was quite valuable.
MID_EV12_026_m01_023: <ACB>I believe I understand well enough.
MID_EV12_026_m01_024: Fabio, hold on there. Are you saying that people\nmade these Grand Megaliths?
MID_EV12_026_m01_025: Of course. The technology required to create\nthem has been lost, however.
MID_EV12_026_m01_026: You know what? I'm starting to think that humans\nare a lot more amazing than I realized.
MID_EV12_026_m01_027: Up till now, I thought only the gods could do\nanything big.
MID_EV12_026_m01_028: And we just float on by it all. It has nothing to do\nwith us.
MID_EV12_026_m01_029: But human history goes back so far... Far, far before\nI was even born.
MID_EV12_026_m01_030: And it'll keep going too, for a long time. I never really\nthought about it.
MID_EV12_026_m01_031: That I would hear such a realization from your lips\nmay be the rarest of my rewards today.
MID_EV12_026_m01_032: What the hell? Even when I get interested, you still\ntalk down to me?
MID_EV12_026_m01_033: I must apologize...for dragging you here.
MID_EV12_026_m01_034: On the contrary. I must thank you.
MID_EV12_026_m01_035: Till now, I had thought that nothing mattered except\npitting myself against the strongest opponents.
MID_EV12_026_m01_036: Those fights were, to me, the same as sating my\nhunger or slaking my thirst.
MID_EV12_026_m01_037: But as we traveled together, and I got to know you...\nYou have changed the way I see the world, if slightly.
MID_EV12_026_m01_038: Fabio, Esmeralda, Mikaela... I owe you my thanks.
MID_EV12_026_m01_039: Well, well! A real smile. Look who's becoming a\nbetter man by the day!
MID_EV12_026_m01_040: Did...did he just say thank you? What's next? A rain\nof frogs?
MID_EV12_026_m01_041: It was my good fortune to meet you. In truth, I ought\nto be the one thanking you.